    <name>
      <text>Solving Exponential and logarithmic inequalities - Question 12a</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p> Solve for \(x\) in the inequality \(\displaystyle {@lhs_const*e^(power*x)@} < {@rhs_const@}\)</p>
<p><b>Note</b>: Give your answer correct to \(2\) decimal places.</p>
<p>\(x< \)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To solve the inequality \({@func@}\) we proceed as follows;</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
\displaystyle {@lhs_const*e^(power*x)@} < {@rhs_const@}\\
&={@e^(power*x)@} < {@rhs_const/lhs_const@}\\
&={@log(e^(power*x))@} <{@log(rhs_const/lhs_const)@}\\
&=x < \displaystyle \frac{{@log(rhs_const/lhs_const)@}}{{@power@}}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<p>Calculating \(\displaystyle \frac{{@log(rhs_const/lhs_const)@}}{{@power@}}\) to two decimalplaces,</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{{@log(rhs_const/lhs_const)@}}{{@power@}}\approx {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p>Therefore,</p>
<p>\(x< {@ta1@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
